<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 1 — THE FOUR WAYS TO RUN
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="s1">
<h2><span class="snum">01</span> The Four Ways to Run Silmulator</h2>

<p>Every launch path ultimately runs the same Python entry point — <code>silmulator/app.py:main()</code> — called via <code>main.py</code>. What differs is <em>how</em> the dependencies are installed and <em>how</em> the display is set up.</p>

<div class="methods">
  <div class="method">
    <h4><span class="ptag p-all">ALL</span> <span class="method-badge">Dev mode</span></h4>
    <p>Clone + pip/uv install deps + <code>python main.py</code>. Fastest for development; no packaging step.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="method">
    <h4><span class="ptag p-docker">Docker</span> <span class="method-badge">Browser</span></h4>
    <p><code>docker compose up</code>, then open <code>localhost:6080</code>. Runs on any OS with no display drivers.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="method">
    <h4><span class="ptag p-mac">macOS</span> <span class="method-badge">Installer</span></h4>
    <p><code>build_installer.sh</code> → <code>.dmg</code>. Drag <code>Silmulator.app</code> to Applications; launch like any app.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="method">
    <h4><span class="ptag p-win">Windows</span> <span class="method-badge">Installer</span></h4>
    <p><code>build_installer.bat</code> → <code>.exe</code> (NSIS) or <code>.zip</code>. Run the installer; start from Start Menu.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="methods">
  <div class="method">
    <h4><span class="ptag p-lnx">Linux</span> <span class="method-badge">AppImage</span></h4>
    <p><code>build_installer.sh</code> → <code>.AppImage</code>. Mark executable; double-click or run from terminal.</p>
  </div>
</div>

