</section>

<!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     SECTION 5 — COMPARISON TABLE
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section id="s5">
<h2><span class="snum">05</span> Comparison — When to Use Which</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Method</th>
      <th>Python needed?</th>
      <th>Needs display?</th>
      <th>Best for</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>python main.py</code></td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Yes</td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Native display</td>
      <td>Active development on any OS</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>uv run python main.py</code></td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Yes (uv handles venv)</td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Native display</td>
      <td>Dev — fastest first-time setup</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>silmulator</code> (installed)</td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Yes</td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Native display</td>
      <td>Dev on a configured machine</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Docker (browser / NoVNC)</td>
      <td><span class="cross">✗</span> No</td>
      <td><span class="cross">✗</span> No — browser only</td>
      <td>CI, remote machines, any OS with zero setup</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Docker (dev / X11 forward)</td>
      <td><span class="cross">✗</span> No</td>
      <td><span class="warn">~</span> X11 server needed</td>
      <td>Dev inside container, live code edits</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>.dmg / .AppImage / .exe</td>
      <td><span class="cross">✗</span> No — self-contained</td>
      <td><span class="tick">✓</span> Native display</td>
      <td>Distributing to end users with no Python</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="callout tip" style="margin-top:1.2rem">
  <span class="callout-icon">💡</span>
  <div><strong>Often confused:</strong> Docker NoVNC mode vs X11 forwarding. <strong>NoVNC</strong> renders inside a full virtual X11 session inside the container and streams it to the browser — no local X server needed, works on any OS. <strong>X11 forwarding</strong> (dev mode) sends Qt draw calls to your local X server — faster and feels more native, but requires XQuartz (Mac), VcXsrv (Win), or a running X11 server (Linux).</div>
</div>

